  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 245 AM EDT Tue Sep 22 2026\n\n- Slight chance of a rain shower South on Wednesday\n\nWe continue to see the upper low over Eastern Iowa as of this \nmorning, continue to weaken and lose its moisture and associated \nprecipitation. The frontal system that was the focus of the heavy \nrain over the region this past weekend, has now completely \nseparated, and the dry low level flow from the NE eat away at much \nof the rain.\n\nToday looks to be a dry day, while the best small chance of rain \nlooks to be over the south on Wednesday afternoon.\n\nWe look to have some diurnal cumulus development again today, but \nnot as extensive as yesterday. This is likely due to the upper level \ntemps moderating, and resulting instability weaker. We continue to \nhave fairly dry conditions below 15k ft, minus the cumulus clouds. \nForecast soundings show this well. There will not be much vertical \ndevelopment with a fairly strong inversion around 4-5k ft, \nespecially with low boundary layer dew points.\n\nThis changes a bit later tonight and Wednesday for southern areas. \nMost model guidance indicates that some low level moisture will \nrotate around the low to our south and up and over the southern \nportion of the forecast area. This added moisture in conjunction \nwith weak short waves in the vicinity will be just enough for a few \nlight showers.  \n\n- Dry weather with slowly warming temperatures into next week\n\nThe amplification of the upper air pattern is still expected to \ntake shape with the low expanding over the Eastern Seaboard, and the \nupper ridge building to our west over the upper Plains. It might be \ntaking a little longer for everything to fall in place than \npreviously thought, which is fairly common with upper lows. It still \nlooks like we will see the upper ridging build over the area, and \nhold in place through early next week. We will be under the \nconfluent flow downstream of the ridge, providing plenty of \nsubsidence for the area.\n\nTemperatures again will remain cool through Wednesday with the upper \nlow and cold pool aloft nearby. Temperatures will moderate then as \nwarmer air builds in and we see much more sunshine.",
